        "operation": "download"
      },
      "typeVersion": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "0d2ea8dc-3014-4760-bd58-5de22a87807d",
      "name": "Sticky Note8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        896,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 344,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## File Retrieval\n\n**Download File from Drive** \u2013 Downloads the validated file from Google Drive using fileId and passes the binary content into the document processing and vector ingestion pipeline."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "47ae2323-cfb9-435e-a10d-f5d089d0a37a",
      "name": "Sticky Note9",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1296,
        -32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1008,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## Document Processing & Vector Ingestion\n\nThis section converts the downloaded file into searchable vectors in Pinecone.\n\n**Parse Document Content** \u2013 Loads binary file content into text and attaches metadata (fileId, fileName, mimeType, source, folderId, modifiedTime, documentVersion) to every chunk.\n\n**Split Text into Chunks** \u2013 Uses a Recursive Character Text Splitter (chunk size 1000, overlap 150) so embeddings stay focused and retrieval stays accurate.\n\n**Generate Embeddings (Ingest)** \u2013 Creates OpenAI embeddings for each chunk.\n\n**Ingest into Pinecone Vector DB** \u2013 Stores vectors in index `n8n-new` under namespace `n8n-rag`."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "203f3ebb-311a-4b7d-89ca-04296b079455",
      "name": "Sticky Note10",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        704
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 996,
        "height": 824,
        "content": "## Query Entry, Validation & AI Agent\n\nThis section receives user questions and prepares a grounded RAG answer.\n\n**User Query Webhook** \u2013 Accepts POST requests on path `pinecone-chat-flow`.\n\n**Validate & Normalize Query** \u2013 Requires a non-empty `question` string, trims formatting, and reads optional `sessionId`, `userId`, and `organizationId`.\n\n**Query Valid?** \u2013 Routes invalid requests directly to the response node with an error payload. Valid requests continue to the AI Agent.\n\n**AI Agent** \u2013 Uses Primary LLM (Agent Brain), Conversation Memory Buffer (dynamic sessionId), and Vector Search QA Tool with a strict RAG system prompt so answers stay based on retrieved documents only."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f65d2d96-2032-4832-a8bf-4b0f0cee1a1b",
      "name": "Sticky Note11",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1120,
        1072
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 792,
        "height": 676,
        "content": "## Response Delivery\n\n**Format RAG Response** \u2013 Builds JSON: success, question, answer, sessionId, and sources.\n\n**Respond to Webhook** \u2013 Returns that payload to the caller.\n\nNote: `sources` is included for a stable API shape. With the current Vector Search QA Tool path, detailed chunk citations are not always available, so `sources` may be an empty array. The answer still comes from retrieved Pinecone context via the agent tool."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
