    {
      "id": "8958db1c-4fe5-47aa-a614-7469cc221f2a",
      "name": "Vector Search QA Tool1",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.toolVectorStore",
      "position": [
        624,
        2000
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "description": "Search the knowledge base for factual information. Use this tool for every user question that needs document-based facts. Return only information found in retrieved documents."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "70339081-3a80-4c97-ae19-4c742386a8a7",
      "name": "Sticky Note13",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -944,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 868,
        "height": 1088,
        "content": "## Workflow Overview & Setup Guide\n\nWho it's for: teams building a private knowledge assistant over Google Drive docs \u2014 support, internal docs, SaaS help centers, and RAG chatbots.\n\nWhat it does: syncs Drive files into Pinecone with metadata, then answers webhook questions using only retrieved knowledge (strict RAG).\n\nHow it works:\n1) Ingestion: Drive File Watcher \u2192 Extract File Metadata \u2192 Validate File \u2192 Download File from Drive \u2192 Parse Document Content \u2192 Split Text into Chunks \u2192 Generate Embeddings (Ingest) \u2192 Ingest into Pinecone Vector DB\n2) Query: User Query Webhook \u2192 Validate & Normalize Query \u2192 Query Valid? \u2192 AI Agent (Primary LLM, Conversation Memory Buffer, Vector Search QA Tool) \u2192 Format RAG Response \u2192 Respond to Webhook\n\nSetup:\n1. Connect Google Drive, OpenAI, and Pinecone credentials\n2. Select your Google Drive folder in Drive File Watcher\n3. Set your Pinecone index and namespace (examples in this template: n8n-new / n8n-rag)\n4. Activate the workflow\n5. POST to webhook path pinecone-chat-flow with { \"question\": \"...\", \"sessionId\": \"optional\" }\n\nRequirements: n8n, Google Drive OAuth, OpenAI API, Pinecone index\n\nCustomize: chunk size/overlap, supported mime types, models, Pinecone index/namespace, and the AI Agent system prompt\n\nSupported files: PDF, DOCX, DOC, TXT, MD, CSV\n\nNote: sources in the JSON response is reserved for citation metadata; it may be empty depending on retrieval metadata availability."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f11a68ba-55b8-4d06-af77-4de8c1f071db",
      "name": "Validate File1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        560,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "leftValue": "",
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "d227e3c6-3b29-492a-ac66-550c711f0bab",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.fileId && $json.fileName && $json.mimeType && ['application/pdf','application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document','application/msword','text/plain','text/markdown','text/csv','application/csv','application/vnd.google-apps.document'].includes($json.mimeType) }}",
              "rightValue": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "a39e0960-62cc-42b4-8167-5e5ef7cb72a1",
      "name": "Validate & Normalize Query1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        288,
        1136
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const body = $json.body || $json;\nconst raw = body.question;\nconst sessionId = body.sessionId || ('session-' + $execution.id);\n\nif (raw === undefined || raw === null || typeof raw !== 'string' || !raw.trim()) {\n  return [{\n    json: {\n      success: false,\n      error: 'Invalid request',\n      message: 'question is required',\n      isValid: false,\n      sessionId\n    }\n  }];\n}\n\nconst question = raw.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\nif (question.length > 4000) {\n  return [{\n    json: {\n      success: false,\n      error: 'Invalid request',\n      message: 'question exceeds maximum length of 4000 characters',\n      isValid: false,\n      sessionId\n    }\n  }];\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    isValid: true,\n    question,\n    sessionId,\n    userId: body.userId || '',\n    organizationId: body.organizationId || '',\n    body: { question, sessionId, userId: body.userId || '', organizationId: body.organizationId || '' }\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "2a1bd627-50c2-4fa9-ad64-03e31992ce89",
      "name": "Query Valid?1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        448,
        1136
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
